keep the "Clockwise Spiral" rule in mind when parsing C declarations.

For example 

<1>
int a[3] = { 2, 3, 4 }

"a" is an array (size_3)  of integer

<2>
int *a[3]

"a" is an array (size_3) of pointers to integers.
<cool so its an array of pointers>

<3>
int (*a)[3]

"a" is a pointer to an array (size_3) of integers.
<cool so its a pointer to an integer array of size 3)



Now lets work it backwards:
We want an "a" such that:
"a" is a pointer to an array of pointers to array (size_3) of integers"

  int (*(*a)[])[3]
